    "title": "Hypothetical RAG Sanity Check: Comparing Retrieval On vs. Off for Local LLMs",
    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical experiment for sanity-checking Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) setups with local LLMs. The scenario involves using 30 local documents as a knowledge base. The core idea is to compare model responses under two distinct conditions: retrieval enabled and retrieval disabled, using the exact same set of questions. This direct comparison aims to highlight the impact of the retrieval component on answer generation. It's important to note that this is a hypothetical experiment, and no actual accuracy results or benchmarks are available. The methodology should accommodate questions that may not have answers within the provided documents, allowing for observation of how the RAG system (or the base LLM without retrieval) handles such cases. The goal is to provide a framework for evaluating RAG effectiveness without relying on pre-existing performance data.",
