    "title": "Designing a Hypothetical RAG Evaluation for Local LLMs: Retrieval On vs. Off",
    "body": "We propose a hypothetical framework for evaluating the sanity of a RAG system operating with local LLMs. The setup is designed around a corpus of 30 local documents. The central tenet of this hypothetical evaluation is a direct comparison: posing the same questions to the LLM with RAG retrieval enabled, and then with retrieval explicitly turned off. This contrast is intended to isolate and demonstrate the contribution of the retrieval mechanism. Crucially, this remains a hypothetical exercise; no real-world measurements or accuracy figures are generated or presented. The proposed method must also account for questions that lack corresponding answers within the 30 documents, observing how both configurations (retrieval on/off) respond to such queries. The objective is to conceptualize a basic RAG validation process, emphasizing the comparison of retrieval's influence on output quality.",
